    {
      "text": "I make an abridgment of the record of my father, upon plates, 1 Ne. 1:17. Lehi, took the records which were engraven upon the plates of brass, 1 Ne. 5:10 (Alma 37:3). they are not the plates upon which I make a full account, 1 Ne. 9:2 (19:3; Jacob 1:1–2, 4; 3:13–14; W of M 1:3–7; D&C 10:41). the plates upon which I make a full account of my people, 1 Ne. 9:2 (19:2; 2 Ne. 4:14; 5:33; Jacob 1:3; 3:13; Morm. 2:18; D&C 10:39). write a few words upon plates, which will give … knowledge concerning us, Jacob 4:2. plates which contained the record of his people from the time that they left the land of Zarahemla, Mosiah 8:5. brought twenty-four plates which are filled with engravings … of pure gold, Mosiah 8:9 (21:27; Alma 37:21; Ether 1:2). plates of Nephi … it is for a wise purpose that they are kept, Alma 37:2. I do make the record on plates which I have made with mine own hands, 3 Ne. 5:11 (Morm. 8:5). I was about to write … upon the plates of Nephi, but the Lord forbade it, 3 Ne. 26:11.",
